                  "description": {
                    "value": "Razor sharp coral growths erupt from the ground, transforming the landscape into a dangerous coral reef.\n\nYou can create a third nonoverlapping burst if the centers of all three bursts are underwater. Creatures in the area when the spell is cast take 6d6 piercing damage and must attempt a basic Reflex save. A creature that critically fails its saving throw also takes 1d6 persistent bleed damage.\n\nThe area becomes 3 and hazardous terrain.\n\nA creature that moves through the area takes 3 piercing damage for every square of that area it moves into."
                  },
                  "higher_level_description": {
                    "value": "Heightened (+2): The initial piercing damage increases by 3d6, and the hazardous terrain damage increases by 1."
                  },
